WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.151
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.201 --> 00:00:06.001
Robotics 101, video 10.

3
00:00:06.051 --> 00:00:08.850
Programming the motors.

4
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.481
Now let us make the robot move.

5
00:00:12.531 --> 00:00:17.976
Before you upload, lift the robot so the wheels are off the table.

6
00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:21.140
That way it cannot drive off the edge.

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.269
This helper drives one motor.

8
00:00:25.319 --> 00:00:30.511
A positive speed sets the direction pins for forward.

9
00:00:30.561 --> 00:00:33.578
A negative speed reverses them.

10
00:00:33.628 --> 00:00:35.655
Zero stops the motor.

11
00:00:35.705 --> 00:00:39.810
analogWrite then sets the speed using PWM.

12
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:46.986
setMotors drives both wheels with one line of code.

13
00:00:47.036 --> 00:00:52.525
Motor A, on ENA, IN1 and IN2, is the left wheel.

14
00:00:52.575 --> 00:00:58.180
Motor B, on ENB, IN3 and IN4, is the right wheel.

15
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:05.218
Try setMotors 150, 150 to go straight.

16
00:01:05.268 --> 00:01:09.130
Try 40, 150 to curve left.

17
00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.192
Try 150, 40 to curve right.

18
00:01:13.242 --> 00:01:15.750
And 0, 0 to stop.

19
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:21.045
If a wheel spins backwards when it should go forward, swap that

20
00:01:21.095 --> 00:01:25.091
motor's two wires at the motor driver, then test again with the

21
00:01:25.141 --> 00:01:25.990
wheels lifted.

22
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.775
Let us recap.

23
00:01:28.825 --> 00:01:33.054
setMotors(left, right) drives both wheels.

24
00:01:33.104 --> 00:01:37.537
Positive forward, negative backward, 0 stop.

25
00:01:37.587 --> 00:01:41.714
Test with the robot lifted off the table.

26
00:01:41.764 --> 00:01:45.280
Next: The line-following algorithm.
